  <name>Myna</name>
  <summary>Local, offline speech-to-text for the desktop</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Myna provides local, offline speech-to-text for the Linux desktop.
      Activate dictation with a hotkey, speak, and the transcript is typed
      into the focused application via IBus. Audio is captured by this app;
      the inference backends have no microphone access. Nothing leaves the
      machine and no audio is persisted.
    </p>
    <p>
      Requires a backend Flatpak to be installed and running:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>com.canonical.Myna.Whisper — Whisper (faster-whisper / CTranslate2)</li>
      <li>com.canonical.Myna.Parakeet — Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 (onnxruntime)</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">com.canonical.Myna.desktop</launchable>
